@*
    OdsTooltip — a hover / focus label on an inverted bubble
    (Odyssey Design System · components/Tooltip).

    Wrap any single focusable trigger; the bubble shows on hover and on keyboard
    focus. A MudTooltip — keep Label terse (one line). Touch is not a tooltip
    surface; put essential info in a visible label instead. ShowOnClick opens it
    on a tap as well, for an info button whose note is not essential.

    LabelContent replaces the text with structured markup (the design's `label` node) — for an info
    note with a lead, rows and a footnote. Label stays required: a structured bubble is not linked
    to its trigger, so the caller still needs the plain text for the trigger's aria-describedby.
*@

<MudTooltip Text="@Label"
            TooltipContent="LabelContent"
            Arrow="true"
            ShowOnClick="ShowOnClick"
            Class="@Class"
            @attributes="UserAttributes">
    @ChildContent
</MudTooltip>

@code {
    /// <summary>The tooltip text. Keep it short — one line.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Label { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>Structured bubble content, drawn instead of <see cref="Label"/>'s text when set.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? LabelContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The trigger element the tooltip describes.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Also opens on a click or tap. For a tooltip that carries a note rather than repeating a label (an info
    /// button), so a touch screen, which has no hover, can reach it.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public bool ShowOnClick { get; set; }

    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public Dictionary<string, object>? UserAttributes { get; set; }
}
